# skill: tabs

## Contract

Tabbed navigation component that displays a list of tab buttons and associated content panels. Only one tab may be active at a time. Clicking a tab switches the visible panel and highlights the selected tab button.

**Inputs:**
- `tabs`: Array of tab objects, each with `value` (string), `label` (string), and `children` (react nodes for React variant)
- `defaultTab`: Initial active tab value (optional, defaults to first tab)

**Outputs:**
- Active tab panel is visible; all others are hidden
- Active tab button shows visual selected state (blue border-bottom, bold text)

**Behavior:**
- Clicking a tab button sets that tab as active
- Only one tab is active at a time
- Panel visibility toggles based on active state
- No external state management required (self-contained)

## Dependencies

- `button-primary` — tab buttons inherit button base styles

## Slots

None.

## Boundaries

- HTML/React only — no SSR considerations for this component
- Assumes `display: none` toggle for panel visibility (not conditional rendering) to preserve DOM structure
- No keyboard navigation or ARIA roles beyond basic `role="tablist"`

## Examples

**Example 1: Basic three tabs**

```jsx
<Tabs
  tabs={[
    { value: 'tab1', label: '標籤一', children: <p>內容一</p> },
    { value: 'tab2', label: '標籤二', children: <p>內容二</p> },
    { value: 'tab3', label: '標籤三', children: <p>內容三</p> },
  ]}
/>
```

**Example 2: With defaultTab**

```jsx
<Tabs
  defaultTab="tab2"
  tabs={[
    { value: 'tab1', label: '標籤一', children: <p>內容一</p> },
    { value: 'tab2', label: '標籤二', children: <p>內容二</p> },
    { value: 'tab3', label: '標籤三', children: <p>內容三</p> },
  ]}
/>
```

[html]
<div class="tabs" id="tab-container">
  <div class="tab-list" role="tablist">
    <button class="tab-btn active" data-tab="tab1" onclick="switchTab('tab1')">標籤一</button>
    <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab2" onclick="switchTab('tab2')">標籤二</button>
    <button class="tab-btn" data-tab="tab3" onclick="switchTab('tab3')">標籤三</button>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-panels">
    <div class="tab-panel active" id="tab1-panel">內容一</div>
    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab2-panel" style="display:none">內容二</div>
    <div class="tab-panel" id="tab3-panel" style="display:none">內容三</div>
  </div>
</div>

[react]
const Tabs = ({ tabs = [], defaultTab }) => {
  const [active, setActive] = React.useState(defaultTab || tabs[0]?.value);
  return (
    <div className="tabs">
      <div className="tab-list" role="tablist">
        {tabs.map(tab => (
          <button key={tab.value} className={"tab-btn" + (active === tab.value ? " active" : "")} onClick={() => setActive(tab.value)}>{tab.label}</button>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div className="tab-panels">
        {tabs.map(tab => (
          <div key={tab.value} className={"tab-panel" + (active === tab.value ? " active" : "")} style={{ display: active === tab.value ? 'block' : 'none' }}>
            {tab.children}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

[style]
.tabs { border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
.tab-list { display: flex; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; background: #fafafa; }
.tab-btn {
  padding: 14px 24px;
  border: none;
  background: transparent;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 500;
  color: #6b7280;
  transition: all 0.15s;
  border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
  margin-bottom: -1px;
}
.tab-btn:hover { color: #374151; }
.tab-btn.active { color: #3b82f6; border-bottom-color: #3b82f6; background: #fff; }
.tab-panels { padding: 20px; }
.tab-panel { display: none; }
.tab-panel.active { display: block; }
